      "repair_reason": "structured ClawSweeper needs-human verdict with repairable P-severity findings (sha=96910fae94ddd107dfdceb8d2b8a475300a737df)",
      "review_summary": "The branch caps gateway `BOOT.md` reads at 16 MiB, resolves readable symlinks before reading, and adds oversized-file, non-regular-file, and readable-symlink coverage.\n\nPR surface: Source +35, Tests +34. Total +69 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. at source level: a dangling symlink makes `realpath` return `ENOENT`, `lstat` then confirms the link exists, and the new branch rethrows instead of returning missing. The provided A/B and runtime evidence also reproduce the intended oversized and readable-symlink paths.",
      "review_followup": "- [P2] A mechanical two-file repair can preserve the established missing-file contract and add dangling-symlink coverage without requiring product, ownership, or security judgment; unrelated dependency drift should remain outside this PR.",
